    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32993": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of the Practice",
      "description": "Duke University, Biology Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Biology Position ID: Duke-Biology-APP_SH [#32993] Position Title: Assistant Professor of the Practice Position Type: Other Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Biology Appl Deadline: ( accepting applications posted 2026/10/07 , updated 2026/10/13 , listed until 2027/04/07) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Department of Biology at Duke University in Durham, North Carolina, invites applications for an Ecologist for an Assistant Professor of the Practice (PoP) position. Specifically, we seek a scholar or practitioner who will advance the understanding of climate and/or sustainability, with opportunities to connect to major teaching and service initiatives as part of Duke’s Climate Commitment (climate.duke.edu). The successful candidate will contribute to the department’s mission through teaching, service, and scholarship. The expectation is that they will teach or co-teach two courses each semester, including courses in introductory ecology and quantitative ecology. The type of scholarship the PoP pursues is flexible (e.g., disciplinary, pedagogical, or course-based research). The initial appointment runs from July 1, 2027 through June 30, 2031 with opportunities for renewal and promotion. This is a regular rank, career track faculty position and is not eligible for tenure. Duke Biology is the intellectual home for more than 50 faculty members whose research programs span the discipline of Biology (including developmental biology, cell biology, molecular biology, ecology, evolution, organismal biology, and genomics). The department graduates ~175 students annually with more than half of our majors conducting independent research. Learn more about Duke Biology at biology.duke.edu. How to Apply: Applicants should hold a Ph.D. degree in biology or a related field, have teaching experience, and should submit the following required documents: · Cover Letter: This one-page document is your first introduction to the department and the search committee. Be specific but brief in explaining your interest in the position, your pertinent skills and vision, and a summary of what makes you a competitive applicant. Include your contact information, and if comfortable, add your preferred name and pronouns. ● Curriculum Vitae: The CV is a document that describes your career trajectory to date. You should include details about where you have completed previous academic training, lists of publications and presentations, awards and grants received, courses taught, and service activities conducted. ● Teaching Statement: In this 2-3 page document, you should describe your teaching philosophy, previous experiences (including courses taught), professional development focused on teaching, and future plans for teaching at the undergraduate levels. We are interested in candidates who not only have experience implementing evidence-based pedagogies in their teaching, but who also can provide examples of how their teaching philosophy has led to specific teaching innovations and/or student learning gains. ● Scholarship Statement: This 1-2 page document should focus on your current as well as your future scholarly agenda. Highlight your main accomplishments and discuss the goals of your scholarship. ● Service and Outreach Statement: In one page or less, please share with us your approaches, training, and experiences in service and outreach. ● List of References: Provide a list of the names and contact information for three professional references (no letters are necessary at this time). Applications must be submitted through Academic Jobs Online: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32993 Applications received by November 30, 2026 will be guaranteed consideration, but we will continue to accept applications through December 30, 2026. Only candidates who have completed their Ph.D. at least one month before the start date of June 1, 2027 can be considered. For additional questions or concerns, please contact Dr. Julie Reynolds, Search Committee Chair, biochairs@duke.edu Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching statement Three Professional References Statement Of Scholarship Service/Outreach Statement And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: www.biology.duke.edu 137 Biological Sciences Bldg. Box 90338 Durham NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32333": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Duke University, Biology Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Biology Position ID: Duke-Biology-PA_DS1 [#32333] Position Title: Postdoctoral Associate Position Type: Postdoctoral Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Biology Appl Deadline: (posted 2026/07/20 , listed until 2027/01/20) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Sherwood Lab, part of the Department of Biology at Duke University, is seeking a full-time Postdoctoral Associate to join a research program focused on understanding how cells invade through basement membranes and how basement membranes regulate tissue development, maintenance, aging, and disease. The lab studies basement membranes, specialized extracellular matrices that surround and support tissues and organs. Using the model organism Caenorhabditis elegans, we combine genetics, CRISPR-based genome engineering, live imaging, and quantitative microscopy to investigate how basement membranes are assembled, remodeled, and maintained in vivo. To support these efforts, the postdoctoral associate will learn and perform a variety of experimental procedures including CRISPR-based genome editing, molecular cloning, C. elegans genetics, fluorescence microscopy, live-cell imaging, quantitative image analysis, and molecular biology techniques. The researcher will work closely with the PI and other lab members to support ongoing projects and develop independent research skills. Applicants should be motivated, dependable, highly organized, and able to work effectively within a collaborative research environment. Strong communication skills and careful attention to detail are essential. Minimum requirements: PhD in biology, cell biology, genetics, biochemistry, bioengineering, or a related field. Prior research experience in molecular biology, genetics, microscopy, image analysis, or model organisms is highly desirable. The position is available beginning August 1, 2026, with flexible start dates based on candidate availability. For more information, visit the Sherwood Lab website: https://sites.duke.edu/sherwoodlab/research/?utm_source=chatgpt.com Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three references (no actual letters, just names and email addresses ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: www.biology.duke.edu 137 Biological Sciences Bldg. Box 90338 Durham NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
