    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32972": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Professor in Combinatorics and Related Areas",
      "description": "Duke University, Department of Mathematics Skip to main content ‌ View Jobs Registered Employers Contact Us Help Login Duke University, Department of Mathematics Position ID: Duke-ARPCOMB [#29149, 50004245] Position Title: Assistant Research Professor in Combinatorics and Related Areas Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Areas: Mathematics: Combinatorics; Probability theory and stochastic Processes; Computer Science Appl Deadline: (posted 2026/10/06 , listed until 2027/04/06) Position Description: Apply Position Description Duke University — Durham, North Carolina, USA Anticipated start date: August 2027 Professor Fan Wei invites applications for a Phillip Griffiths Assistant Research Professor in the Department of Mathematics at Duke University. Applicants working in combinatorics, probability, related areas of pure mathematics, theoretical computer science, or the mathematical foundations of data science, machine learning, and artificial intelligence are encouraged to apply. Professor Wei holds a primary appointment in Mathematics and a secondary appointment in Computer Science. The position is supported by Dr. Wei's National Science Foundation grant and Duke’s Department of Mathematics. The initial appointment is for two years, with the possibility of a one-year extension subject to additional funding. Research and professional development The successful candidate will pursue research with Professor Wei in combinatorics, theoretical computer science, other areas in mathematics, and related areas broadly defined. Specific research directions will reflect shared interests and the candidate’s expertise.\r\nThe position offers opportunities for collaboration with researchers in Mathematics and Computer Science, co-mentoring graduate and undergraduate students, and helping organize combinatorics seminars and other research activities at Duke. Teaching The standard teaching load is one course per semester, for a total of two courses per academic year, in the Department of Mathematics. An alternative arrangement involving three courses per academic year and a higher salary may be available by mutual agreement and subject to departmental approval. Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in mathematics, computer science, or a related discipline broadly defined, awarded before August 1, 2027. Candidates should demonstrate strong research potential, initiative, the ability to work both independently and collaboratively, and a commitment to effective teaching. Strong written and oral communication skills are expected.\r\nApplicants from the areas listed above are welcome; research interests or expertise need not align exactly with Dr. Wei’s previous work. Application materials Applicants should submit the following through [application portal/link]:\r\n•\tA cover letter describing their interest in the position and potential research connections \r\n        with Professor Wei.\r\n•\tA research statement.\r\n•\tA teaching statement. \r\n•\tA curriculum vitae.\r\n•\tTwo representative research papers, including published articles or preprints.\r\n•\tAt least 3 letters of recommendation addressing research and 1 additional letter addressing\r\n        teaching, submitted directly by the recommenders. Review of completed applications will begin on December 10, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to fan.wei@duke.edu.\r\nAMS subject classifications: 05, 60, 68. Please note that Duke University specifically seeks information about past\r\nmisconduct or policy violations (in the past ten (10) years) and/or\r\nrelevant pending investigations as part of the application process.\r\nDisclosures will not be an automatic bar to hiring but, instead, will\r\ninitiate further dialogue regarding past actions and steps taken to\r\naddress them. Disclosures will not be shared with search committees\r\nduring the application review process. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Research statement Teaching statement Two representative research papers, including published articles or preprints Four reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.math.duke.edu 919-660-2800 Appointments Committee Department of Mathematics Box 90320 Duke University Durham, NC 27708 © 2026 MathJobs.Org, American Mathematical Society. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32417": {
      "title": "Spanish Language Instructor",
      "description": "Duke University, Department of Romance Studies Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Department of Romance Studies Position ID: Duke-RomanceStudies-SLPFALL26 [#32417] Position Title: Spanish Language Instructor Position Type: Non-regular rank faculty Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Spanish Appl Deadline: 2026/08/19 23:59:59 filled (posted 2026/08/05 , listed until 2027/02/05) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Department of Romance Studies at Duke University is seeking a qualified instructor of beginning and intermediate Spanish language for a one-year appointment. Qualifications requested for candidates: PhD in linguistics, literature, language pedagogy, or related areas. This is a full-time position (5 language courses per year) with competitive salary and benefits. We seek candidates with a demonstrated excellence in teaching and curriculum design, a proven ability to work effectively in teams, and a strong interest in working with undergraduate students from diverse backgrounds. Please submit a CV, cover letter, 3 letters of recommendation, and teaching portfolio (statement of teaching philosophy, teaching evaluations, sample syllabi or original teaching materials, and a teaching video, if available). Screening will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Duke is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment opportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or veteran status. Duke makes good faith efforts to recruit, hire, and promote qualified women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, and veterans. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: •     Cover Letter •     Curriculum Vitae •     Statement of Teaching Philosophy •     Transcripts •     Teaching Evaluations •     Teaching Video, if available •     Three Reference Letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers) And anything else requested in the position description. Duke University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment opportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy related conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, innovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich diversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. To achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the community feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all individuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://romancestudies.duke.edu/ 919-660-3101 205 Language Center Box 90257 Durham, NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
