    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32219": {
      "title": "Accounting Faculty Positions",
      "description": "Duke University, Fuqua School of Business (Faculty) Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Fuqua School of Business (Faculty) Position ID: Duke-Fuqua School of Business (Faculty)-ACCOUNTING [#32219] Position Title: Accounting Faculty Positions Position Type: Tenured/Tenure-track faculty Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Accounting Appl Deadline: 2026/11/15 23:59:59  (posted 2026/06/18 , listed until 2026/11/15) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Fuqua School of Business, Duke University is seeking to fill one tenure track faculty position at the assistant professor level in accounting, beginning with the 2027-2028 academic year, subject to university approval. Candidates should have a PhD in accounting or a related field or be close to completing that degree, excellent research skills in any area of accounting research, and excellent teaching skills. Hiring decisions will be based on the candidate's ability to contribute to the research and teaching missions of the Fuqua School of Business, with a preference for candidates with teaching interests in financial or managerial accounting.  We will begin to consider applications starting September 10, 2026; application materials should be received no later than November 15, 2026. The Fuqua School of Business is committed to fostering a diverse educational environment and encourages applications from members of groups under-represented in academia. To apply, submit the following required items online at: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32219 •\tCover letter\r\n•\tCurriculum Vitae\r\n•\tResearch statement\r\n•\tTeaching statement\r\n•\tTranscript or diploma showing highest degree awarded\r\n•\tJob market paper\r\n•\tThree reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers at the above site) Further information is availab