    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32106": {
      "title": "Operations Management Faculty Position",
      "description": "Duke University, Fuqua School of Business (Faculty) Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Fuqua School of Business (Faculty) Position ID: Duke-Fuqua School of Business (Faculty)-OPS [#32106] Position Title: Operations Management Faculty Position Position Type: Tenured/Tenure-track faculty Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Operations Management Appl Deadline: 2026/10/15 23:59:59  (posted 2026/05/26 , listed until 2026/10/30) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Operations Management area at the Fuqua School of Business, Duke University, is seeking applicants for a tenure-track appointment at the Assistant Professor level for the 2027/28 academic year. Applicants should have a Ph.D. or plan to receive one by September 2027, a strong research record, and the ability to teach successfully in our programs. The Fuqua School of Business is a top-rated, highly innovative, global business school.  Duke University is regarded as one of the nation’s finest. The Raleigh-Durham-Chapel Hill area has been highly rated as a living environment by many publications.  The presence of several major universities and the Research Triangle Park technology hub helps to provide an outstanding combination of exceptional lifestyle, vibrant high-tech business community, and an extensive set of cultural, academic, and leisure opportunities.\r\n \r\nInterested candidates should submit their applications electronically via Academic Jobs Online https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32106 Applicants interested in applying should submit a cover letter, vita, samples of research, evidence of teaching effectiveness and three letters of reference. The area will begin reviewing applications at the start of the fall semester, so early submission is encouraged. The deadline for applications is October 15, 2026. For any questions, please contact Professor Fernando Bernstein. Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Please note that Duke University specifically seeks information about past\r\nmisconduct or policy violations (in the past ten (10) years) and/or\r\nrelevant pending investigations as part of the application process.\r\nDisclosures will not be an automatic bar to hiring but, instead, will\r\ninitiate further dialogue regarding past actions and steps taken to\r\naddress them. Disclosures will not be shared with search committees\r\nduring the application review process. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Up to three research papers (published or unpublished) Evidence of teaching effectiveness Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) Further Info: https://areas.fuqua.duke.edu/operations-management/ 100 Fuqua Drive P.O. Box 90120 Durham, NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
