    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32873": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Associate",
      "description": "Duke University, Fuqua School of Business (Faculty) Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Fuqua School of Business (Faculty) Position ID: Duke-Fuqua School of Business (Faculty)-POSTDOCVTRL [#32873] Position Title: Post-Doctoral Associate Position Type: Postdoctoral Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Management and Organizations Appl Deadline: 2026/11/15 23:59:59  (posted 2026/09/29 ) Position Description: Apply Position Description Duke University's Fuqua School of Business invites applications for the position of post-doctoral associate expected to begin January 1, 2027. This is initially a 12-month position with the possibility of renewal or extension contingent on satisfactory performance, continued programmatic need, and availability of funding. The Postdoctoral Associate will conduct behavioral, organizational, and workforce-related research as part of the Veteran Transitions Research Lab (VTRL) at Duke University’s Fuqua School of Business. Working under the guidance of VTRL faculty mentors, the Postdoctoral Associate will contribute to VTRL’s research portfolio while developing an independent program of scholarship. The position will involve study design, evidence synthesis, participant recruitment and data collection, statistical analysis, manuscript preparation, report writing, conference presentations, and practitioner-facing dissemination. Primary responsibilities: The Postdoctoral Associate will conduct behavioral, organizational, and workforce-related research; support study design, literature reviews, participant recruitment, data collection, analysis, and interpretation; prepare scholarly and practitioner-facing materials; manage project timelines and communicate with collaborators; follow applicable research and institutional requirements; and provide mentorship to students or research assistants. Required qualifications: Candidates must have a PhD in a relevant behavioral or social science field, experience designing and analyzing related research, strong scholarly writing and communication skills, and excellent analytical, organizational, project-management, and interpersonal abilities. They must also be able to work independently and collaboratively while demonstrating a commitment to responsible research practices and institutional compliance. For full consideration, applications should be submitted by November 15, 2026. Applicants should submit their materials electronically at: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32873 Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Transcript or diploma of highest degree Two reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) Further Info: Fuqua School of Business 100 Fuqua Drive Duke University, Box 90120 Durham NC  27708-0120 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32905": {
      "title": "Associate in Research",
      "description": "Duke University, Fuqua School of Business (Faculty) Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Fuqua School of Business (Faculty) Position ID: Duke-Fuqua School of Business (Faculty)-RAFIN [#32905] Position Title: Associate in Research Position Type: Other Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Finance / Corporate Appl Deadline: 2027/01/20 23:59:59  (posted 2026/10/01 , listed until 2027/01/20) Position Description: Apply Position Description Research Associate position at Duke University's Fuqua School of Business, Finance Area The Finance Area at Duke University's Fuqua School of Business is seeking talented and driven individuals for a full-time Research Associate position for a minimum of one year. Applications will be reviewed starting in February 2027. This role offers the unique advantage of working collaboratively with several faculty members, providing a dynamic and diverse experience across various finance areas. Responsibilities include statistical analysis, data scraping, and literature reviews, using tools like Stata, MATLAB, Python, and R. Ideal candidates should have a strong quantitative and programming background, with the ability to work independently. A background in economics or finance is helpful but not required. This position is perfect for those seeking to deepen their empirical and theoretical knowledge in economics or finance, preparing for graduate studies. Applications should include a short cover letter, a current CV, and academic transcripts. Applicants should submit their materials electronically at https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32905 . Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. To be given full consideration, please submit your application by January 20, 2027. Any further inquiries should be sent to predoc_finance@duke.edu. Starting date is July 1, 2027. Competitive salaries and standard benefits are offered. Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://areas.fuqua.duke.edu/finance/ Fuqua School of Business 100 Fuqua Drive Duke University, Box 90120 Durham, NC  27708-0120 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
