    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32866": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in German Studies and Slavic and Eurasian Studies",
      "description": "Duke University, German Studies, and<br>Slavic and Eurasian Studies Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, German Studies, and Slavic and Eurasian Studies Position ID: Duke-GermanStudies-ASSISTANTPROFESSOR [#32866] Position Title: Assistant Professor in German Studies and Slavic and Eurasian Studies Position Type: Tenured/Tenure-track faculty Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Areas: Germanic Languages and Literatures Russian, Eurasian, and East European Studies Starting Date: 2027/07/01 Appl Deadline: 2026/11/15 23:59:59 * * (posted 2026/09/29 ) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Departments of German Studies and of Slavic and Eurasian Studies at Duke University in Durham, North Carolina, invite applications for a tenure-track position at the assistant professor level beginning July 1, 2027, with an initial appointment through June 30, 2031, renewable upon successful review. Exceptional research agenda and commitment to teaching excellence required in both German Studies and a Slavic or Eurasian field of expertise, including fluency in both of the research languages. We are seeking a scholar in 20th- and 21st-century literature, culture, film, and/or media, and expect that the position will strengthen ties between the two programs. PhD in hand by June 30, 2027, from a department of German Studies, of Slavic Studies, of Comparative Literature, or similar field. Teaching at both graduate and undergraduate levels expected. Applicants should submit an application letter, a CV, three letters of recommendation, and a writing sample (max 25 pages) through Academic Jobs Online: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32866 . Dossiers received by November 15, 2026, are guaranteed consideration. For questions about the position, please contact the chair of the search committee, Stefani Engelstein (stefani.engelstein@duke.edu). Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Please note that Duke University specifically seeks information about past\r\nmisconduct or policy violations (in the past ten (10) years) and/or\r\nrelevant pending investigations as part of the application process.\r\nDisclosures will not be an automatic bar to hiring but, instead, will\r\ninitiate further dialogue regarding past actions and steps taken to\r\naddress them. Disclosures will not be shared with search committees\r\nduring the application review process. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Writing Sample - max 25 pages Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://german.duke.edu/ Duke University German Studies Department BOX 90256 116A Old Chem Durham, NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
