    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32934": {
      "title": "Associate in Research",
      "description": "Duke University, Physics Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Physics Position ID: Duke-Physics-AIRGAO [#32934, 51228444] Position Title: Associate in Research Position Type: Other Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Physics Appl Deadline: 2026/10/10 23:59:59  (posted 2026/10/02 ) Position Description: Apply Position Description Position Description:\r\nThe Medium Energy Physics Group in the Department of Physics at Duke University invites applications for an Associate in Research position. The successful candidates will work with Prof. Haiyan Gao. \r\nThis position will involve analyzing data from the JLab Hall D SRC/CT experiment and carrying out related studies on  and J/ meson production to explore the extraction of the mass radius of the deuteron, and the transition from nucleon-meson degrees of freedom to quark-gluon degrees of QCD. The successful applicant will also work on drafting publications on the outcome of these studies and documenting the required analysis and simulation codes.\r\nRequired Qualifications:\r\n●\tBachelor’s degree in physics or a related field by the start date. Master’s or Ph.D. preferred.\r\nEnvironment and Collaboration:\r\nDuke University is in Durham, North Carolina, a thriving area with an excellent quality of life and strong academic networks across the Research Triangle.\r\nApplication Instructions:\r\nApplicants should submit the following materials as a single PDF to AJO:\r\n1.\tCover letter outlining research interests and qualifications 2.\tCurriculum vitae including publications 3.\tBrief research statement (≤3 pages) 4.\tContact information for three references\r\nReview of applications will begin October 2, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Informal inquiries are welcome and may be sent to Dr. Haiyan Gao (hgao@duke.edu). Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Research statement Three references (no actual letters, just names and email addresses ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: www.phy.duke.edu Duke University Physics Department Box 90305 Durham, NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32936": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Duke University, Physics Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Physics Position ID: Duke-Physics-POSDOCBASS [#32936, 51229604] Position Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate Position Type: Postdoctoral Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Physics / Physics Appl Deadline: 2026/12/31 23:59:59  (posted 2026/10/02 ) Position Description: Apply Position Description The QCD Group in the Department of Physics at Duke University invites applications for a Postdoctoral Research Associate position. The successful candidates will work with Profs. Steffen A. Bass and Berndt Mueller. Topics of interest include, but are not limited to: perturbative QCD, Quark-Gluon-Plasma Phenomenology, Transport Theory of Relativistic Heavy-Ion Collisions, Jet and heavy-flavor physics, initial state dynamics, QCD transport coefficients, the application of Bayesian statistics and ML/AI to the modeling of relativistic heavy-ion collisions and all areas of QCD with applications related to the Heavy-Ion program at RHIC and LHC as well as the e-A program at the EIC. To be considered for the position, the candidate’s research statement needs to outline how their research will fit with or complement the current research by the Duke QCD group led by Steffen A. Bass and Berndt Mueller. \r\nThe research group currently consists of the two faculty, one postdoc and 3 graduate students. The successful candidate is expected to actively engage with other members of the group and participate in the mentoring of the graduate students. Required Qualifications:\r\n● Ph.D. in physics or a related field by the start date and have expertise in an area relevant to the group's research program Environment and Collaboration:\r\nDuke University is in Durham, North Carolina, a thriving area with an excellent quality of life and strong academic networks across the Research Triangle. Application Instructions:\r\nApplicants should submit the following materials as a single PDF to AJO:\r\n1.\tCover letter outlining research interests and qualifications 2.\tCurriculum vitae including publications 3.\tBrief research statement (≤3 pages) 4.\tContact information for three references Review of applications will begin January 1, 2027, and will continue until the position is filled. Informal inquiries are welcome and may be sent to Dr. Steffen Bass (bass@duke.edu). Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Research statement Publication list Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site. Letters should be submitted by 2026/07/31 11:59PM ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: www.phy.duke.edu Duke University Physics Department Box 90305 Durham, NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32781": {
      "title": "AI for Product Innovation Executive Director",
      "description": "Duke University, Pratt Masters Programs Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Pratt Masters Programs Position ID: Duke-GSF-AIPIEXECDIR [#32781] Position Title: AI for Product Innovation Executive Director Position Type: Non-regular rank faculty Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Areas: Artificial Intelligence Engineering Appl Deadline: 2026/10/31 23:59:59  (posted 2026/09/21 , listed until 2027/03/21) Position Description: Apply Position Description Executive Director\r\nof Master of Engineering in AI for Product Innovation (Executive in Residence)\r\nJob Description Duke University’s Pratt School\r\nof Engineering is seeking a talented, driven, and innovative Executive\r\nDirector to lead the Master of Engineering in AI\r\nfor Product Innovation Program . This is a full-time, on-site\r\nposition based in Durham, NC. The program is designed to prepare students for\r\nleadership in the complex and evolving world of artificial intelligence through\r\ninterdisciplinary expertise, technical acumen, innovative problem-solving\r\nskills, and strong leadership abilities. Position\r\nOverview The\r\nmajor responsibilities of the Executive Director will be to (1) to lead the\r\nMaster of Engineering in AIPI and (2) teach two courses per year. In this role,\r\nyou will be expected to: Program leadership on initiatives related to curriculum design,\r\n     program assessment, and admissions review. Enhance\r\n     and oversee a world-class interdisciplinary academic program including\r\n     managing faculty, operations, and budget, while creating a collaborative\r\n     and respectful work environment. Collaborate across program, institute, department, and school\r\n     boundaries. Identify and hire innovative faculty to teach the curriculum. Develop and deliver innovative and applied, problem-based courses. Support the development of co-curricular programs for students. Develop\r\n     a long-term vision and implement strategic plans that further enhance the\r\n     residential and online AIPI program. Promote the program to external constituencies. Direct student recruiting and student admissions process. Lead industry engagement by cultivating and maintaining\r\n     relationships with industry partners to enhance student learning,\r\n     project-based experiences, and career opportunities. Promote growth and management of initiatives such as labs,\r\n     experiential learning, or applied research that connect academic\r\n     preparation with industry practice. Qualifications Ideal candidates will have at least ten years of experience in technical\r\nand managerial roles in either an academic, government or corporate setting.\r\nCandidates should also demonstrate strong communication skills, a collaborative\r\nspirit, and a passion for mentoring emerging professionals. A master’s degree in\r\na relevant technical discipline is required, with a doctorate or terminal\r\ndegree preferred. In exceptional cases, significant and highly relevant\r\nindustry experience may be considered in place of a doctorate degree. Candidate\r\nshould demonstrate teaching experience, preferably in a higher education or\r\nprofessional training setting. Experience in academic program-building,\r\ncurriculum development, or collaborative educational leadership is preferred.\r\nCandidate should have strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the\r\nability to work across academic, industry, and governmental boundaries. This role is part of\r\nthe Institute for Enterprise Engineering , which supports the development of\r\nengineering professionals throughout their careers. The AIPI program combines\r\ntechnical depth in artificial intelligence and machine learning with hands-on\r\nproduct development with strong connections to industry. The program values\r\ncollaboration, innovation, and real-word impact, preparing students to\r\ntranslate emerging AI technologies into products and solutions that address\r\nmeaningful challenges. If you are excited about leading a forward-looking\r\nacademic program, shaping the next generation of AI professionals, building\r\nstrong partnerships with industry, and advancing innovative approaches to\r\napplied AI education, we encourage you to apply. Our institutional\r\nculture is built upon our history and values. Our shared values: respect,\r\ntrust, inclusion, discovery, and excellence are more than aspirations. They are\r\nthe beliefs and behaviors that we expect of ourselves and our colleagues. These\r\nare the ideals that we must uphold in order to earn and maintain our reputation\r\nfor quality and integrity, and to inspire confidence with each other, and the\r\nworld which we both serve and rely on for our future viability. All members of\r\nour community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Information about\r\nDuke Values and Culture can be found at https://president.duke.edu/values/ . Please note that\r\nDuke specifically seeks information about past misconduct or policy violations\r\n(in the past ten (10) years) and/or relevant pending investigations as part of\r\nthe application process. Disclosures will not be an automatic bar to hiring but,\r\ninstead, will initiate further dialogue regarding past actions and steps taken\r\nto address them. Disclosures will not be shared with search committees during\r\nthe application review process. Duke is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment\r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, gender,\r\ngender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race,\r\nreligion, (including pregnancy and pregnancy related conditions), sexual\r\norientation, or military status. Duke aspires to create a community built on collaboration, innovation,\r\ncreativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on the robust\r\nexchange of ideas — an exchange that is best when the rich diversity of our\r\nperspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. To achieve this\r\nexchange, it is essential that all members of the community feel secure and\r\nwelcome, that the contributions of all individuals are respected, and that all\r\nvoices are heard. All members of our community have a responsibility to uphold\r\nthese values. Applicants should submit the materials below for consideration. Applications will be\r\nconsidered until a suitable applicant is found. This is a national search and\r\nthere is potential for relocation assistance for the selected candidate. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online to complete your application: Cover letter Teaching Statement, including\r\n     examples of course topics the candidate could consider teaching, approach\r\n     to creating an exemplary classroom environment and instructional\r\n     approaches to optimize student learning. Curriculum Vitae or Resume Three references (names and email\r\n     addresses only) Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching statement Three references (no actual letters, just names and email addresses ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://pratt.duke.edu/academics/departments/iene/ 110 Science Drive, Teer 305 Box 90271 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32325": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor Cybersecurity",
      "description": "Duke University, Pratt Masters Programs Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Pratt Masters Programs Position ID: Duke-GSF-CYBERADJ1 [#32325] Position Title: Adjunct Professor Cybersecurity Position Type: Non-regular rank faculty Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Areas: Cyber Security Engineering / Security , Cyber-Physical Systems Appl Deadline: filled (posted 2026/07/17 , listed until 2027/01/17) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Pratt School of Engineering at Duke University is seeking a Non-Regular Rank Adjunct Professor to teach Masters-level cybersecurity classes. The ideal candidate will have commitment, passion, and excellence in teaching.\r\n\r\nThis position would teach one class per semester in the areas of Cybersecurity in the Master's program. This role will have the mentorship of Pratt’s outstanding regular-rank teaching faculty and not only polish their teaching skills but also become immersed in the novel pedagogy used in these programs. Successful candidates will be expected to: Develop and oversee a world class interdisciplinary master’s program Teach 2-3 courses each year within the current curriculum Collaborate across department and school boundaries Develop and deliver applications-oriented courses related to the current curriculum Connect and engage with industry partners regarding capstone projects, career opportunities, seminar discussions, and participation in an industrial advisory board Ideal candidates would have Cybersecurity experience in either an academic, government or corporate setting. They would also have a PhD or commensurate industry experience/expertise in a Cybersecurity related discipline, such as Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or Electrical Engineering, as well as teaching/course development experience. Existing industry and or government relations in the Cybersecurity space is highly desirable.\r\n\r\nWe seek staff members committed to building a diverse and inclusive community that fosters excellence in research and teaching and welcome applications from women and members of minority groups as well as others who would bring additional dimensions to the university’s research and teaching missions. Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three references (no actual letters, just names and email addresses ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://pratt.duke.edu/academics/departments/iene/ 110 Science Drive, Teer 305 Box 90271 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32780": {
      "title": "Cybersecurity Executive Director",
      "description": "Duke University, Pratt Masters Programs Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Pratt Masters Programs Position ID: Duke-GSF-CYBEREXECDIR [#32780] Position Title: Cybersecurity Executive Director Position Type: Non-regular rank faculty Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Areas: Cyber Security Engineering / Cyber-Physical Systems Appl Deadline: 2026/10/31 23:59:59  (posted 2026/09/21 , listed until 2027/03/21) Position Description: Apply Position Description Executive Director\r\nof Master of Engineering in Cybersecurity (Executive in Residence) Job\r\nDescription Duke University’s\r\nPratt School of Engineering is seeking a talented, driven, and innovative Executive\r\nDirector to lead the Master of Engineering in Cybersecurity program. This is a full-time,\r\non-site position based in Durham, NC. The program is designed to prepare\r\nstudents for leadership in the complex and evolving world of cybersecurity\r\nthrough interdisciplinary expertise, technical acumen, innovative problem-solving\r\nskills, and strong leadership abilities. Position\r\nOverview The\r\nmajor responsibilities of the Executive Director will be to (1) to lead the\r\nMaster of Engineering in Cybersecurity and (2) teach two courses per year. In\r\nthis role, you will be expected to: · Provide program leadership on initiatives related to curriculum design,\r\nprogram assessment, and admissions review. · Enhance\r\nand oversee a world-class interdisciplinary academic program including managing\r\nfaculty, operations, and budget, while creating a collaborative and respectful\r\nwork environment. · Collaborate across program, institute, department, and school boundaries. · Identify and hire innovative faculty to teach the curriculum. · Develop and deliver innovative and applied, problem-based courses. · Support the development of co-curricular programs and research\r\nopportunities for students. · Develop\r\na long-term vision and implement strategic plans that further enhance the\r\nresidential and online Cybersecurity program. · Promote the program to external constituencies. · Direct student recruiting and student admissions processes. · Lead industry engagement by cultivating and maintaining relationships\r\nwith industry partners to enhance student learning, project-based experiences,\r\nand career opportunities. · Interact with Industry Advisory Board members to develop opportunities for\r\ncollaboration on internships, jobs and research. · Foster and develop relationships with the US military and federal\r\ngovernment agencies to identify and deliver educational and research initiatives. · Promote growth and management of initiatives such as labs, experiential\r\nlearning, or applied research that connect academic preparation with industry\r\npractice. · Maintain and promote the National Security Agency Center of Academic\r\nExcellence designations. · Oversee the Duke Executive Education Certificate program and the Duke\r\nCybersecurity Conference. Qualifications Ideal candidates will have at least ten years of experience in technical\r\nand managerial roles in either an academic, government or corporate setting.\r\nCandidates should also demonstrate strong communication skills, a collaborative\r\nspirit, and a passion for mentoring emerging professionals. A master’s degree\r\nis required, with a doctorate or terminal degree preferred. In exceptional\r\ncases, significant and highly relevant industry experience may be considered in\r\nplace of a doctorate degree. Candidate should demonstrate teaching experience,\r\npreferably in a higher education or professional training setting. Experience\r\nin academic program-building, curriculum development, or collaborative\r\neducational leadership is preferred. Candidate should have strong interpersonal\r\nand communication skills, with the ability to work across academic, industry,\r\nand governmental boundaries. This role is part of\r\nthe Institute for Enterprise Engineering , which supports the development of\r\nengineering professionals throughout their careers. The Cybersecurity program\r\nembraces a collaborative culture, values real-world impact, and thrives at the\r\nintersection of creativity and technology. Our institutional\r\nculture is built upon our history and values. Our shared values: respect,\r\ntrust, inclusion, discovery, and excellence are more than aspirations. They are\r\nthe beliefs and behaviors that we expect of ourselves and our colleagues. These\r\nare the ideals that we must uphold in order to earn and maintain our reputation\r\nfor quality and integrity, and to inspire confidence with each other, and the\r\nworld which we both serve and rely on for our future viability. All members of\r\nour community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Information about\r\nDuke Values and Culture can be found at https://president.duke.edu/values/ . Please note that\r\nDuke specifically seeks information about past misconduct or policy violations\r\n(in the past ten (10) years) and/or relevant pending investigations as part of\r\nthe application process. Disclosures will not be an automatic bar to hiring but,\r\ninstead, will initiate further dialogue regarding past actions and steps taken\r\nto address them. Disclosures will not be shared with search committees during\r\nthe application review process. Duke is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment\r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, gender,\r\ngender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race,\r\nreligion, (including pregnancy and pregnancy related conditions), sexual\r\norientation, or military status. Duke aspires to create a community built on collaboration, innovation,\r\ncreativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on the robust\r\nexchange of ideas — an exchange that is best when the rich diversity of our\r\nperspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. To achieve this\r\nexchange, it is essential that all members of the community feel secure and\r\nwelcome, that the contributions of all individuals are respected, and that all\r\nvoices are heard. All members of our community have a responsibility to uphold\r\nthese values. Applicants should submit the materials below for consideration. The\r\npreferred application deadline is October 31, 2026, but applications will be\r\nconsidered until a suitable applicant is found. This is a national search and\r\nthere is potential for relocation assistance for the selected candidate. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online to complete your application: Cover letter Teaching Statement, including\r\n     examples of course topics the candidate could consider teaching, approach\r\n     to creating an exemplary classroom environment and instructional\r\n     approaches to optimize student learning. Curriculum Vitae or Resume Three references (names and email\r\n     addresses only) Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching statement Three references (no actual letters, just names and email addresses ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://pratt.duke.edu/academics/departments/iene/ 110 Science Drive, Teer 305 Box 90271 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
