    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33024": {
      "title": "Family Medicine Physician",
      "description": "Duke University, Student Affairs, Student Health Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Student Affairs, Student Health Position ID: Duke-Student Affairs, Student Health-FMP [#33024] Position Title: Family Medicine Physician Position Type: Other Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27705, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Physician Salary Range: $180,000 - $190,000 Appl Deadline: open until filled  (posted 2026/10/09 ) Position Description: Apply Position Description Be You. At Duke, we celebrate individuality and the unique\r\nperspectives that each member of our community brings. As a Family Medicine\r\nPhysician with Duke Student Health , you'll play an essential role in\r\nsupporting the health, well-being, and success of more than 19,000\r\nundergraduate, graduate, and professional students. You'll join a collaborative and mission-driven team of\r\nphysicians, advanced practice providers, nurses, and administrative\r\nprofessionals who are dedicated to helping students thrive academically,\r\npersonally, and physically throughout their Duke experience. Whether providing\r\npreventive care, managing chronic conditions, addressing mental health\r\nconcerns, or supporting students through unexpected health challenges, you'll\r\nhave the opportunity to make a lasting impact every day. We welcome physicians who are passionate about caring for\r\nyoung adults, committed to inclusive and patient-centered care, and energized\r\nby working within a dynamic university environment. Be Bold As a faculty physician within Duke Student Health, you'll\r\nhelp shape the future of college health through clinical excellence, education,\r\nquality improvement, and student engagement. You will deliver comprehensive\r\ncare while contributing to innovative programs that advance student wellness\r\nand support a thriving campus community. Position Status: Regular; Full-Time, Exempt, Onsite Schedule/Shift: Monday-Friday 8:00 am – 5:00 pm with\r\noccasional evening and weekend work required for departmental and divisional\r\nevents. Position participates in an after-hours on-call coverage for student\r\nsupport Supervisor: Director, Duke Student Health Staff Supervision: Advanced Practice Providers What\r\nYou'll Do Provide\r\nExceptional Clinical Care (85%) Deliver comprehensive primary and acute care services\r\n     through both in-person and telehealth visits. Conduct physical examinations, diagnostic evaluations,\r\n     treatment planning, and referrals as needed. Provide preventive care, chronic disease management,\r\n     urgent care services, and mental health support relevant to the college\r\n     student population. Maintain accurate, timely, and compliant documentation\r\n     within the electronic health record (EHR). Manage EHR communications and patient follow-up\r\n     activities. Participate in after-hours on-call coverage\r\n     approximately every six to eight weeks in collaboration with the nurse\r\n     triage service. Supervise Advanced Practice Providers in accordance\r\n     with Duke and state requirements, providing consultation, mentorship, and\r\n     performance feedback. Partner with specialists, clinicians, nurses, and staff\r\n     to coordinate high-quality, integrated care. Participate in Student Health and Student Affairs\r\n     initiatives, committees, and programs that support student success. Advance\r\nLearning, Innovation, and Quality (10%) Engage in scholarly activities that contribute to the\r\n     advancement of college health and family medicine. Publish, present, lecture, or participate in\r\n     professional development opportunities when appropriate. Precept Family Medicine, Pediatrics, and Med-Peds\r\n     residents in the Student Health setting. Lead or contribute to quality assessment and quality\r\n     improvement projects that strengthen healthcare delivery and accreditation\r\n     efforts. Develop educational content and participate in campus\r\n     outreach initiatives that promote student wellness. Contribute\r\nto the Duke Community (5%) Support departmental, divisional, and university\r\n     priorities through special projects and additional responsibilities as\r\n     assigned. Foster a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performing\r\n     workplace culture. Serve as a trusted partner in promoting the health and\r\n     flourishing of Duke students. What\r\nYou'll Bring Required\r\nQualifications Education MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school. Successful completion of an accredited Family Medicine\r\n     residency program. Licensure Unrestricted North Carolina medical license or\r\n     eligibility to obtain licensure. Federal DEA registration and North Carolina prescribing\r\n     authority. Certification Board Certified or Board Eligible through the American\r\n     Board of Family Medicine (ABFM). Pending residency graduates are encouraged to apply. Preferred\r\nQualifications Three or more years of experience in primary care,\r\n     urgent care, or related ambulatory practice settings. Previous experience working in college health or\r\n     student health environments. Experience performing common office procedures such as: Suturing Incision and drainage Toenail removal Comfort providing evidence-based mental health\r\n     assessment, management, and medication prescribing. Demonstrated commitment to patient-centered care,\r\n     interprofessional collaboration, and health equity. Choose Duke. At Duke University, you'll find more than a job. You'll\r\ndiscover a community dedicated to excellence, innovation, collaboration, and\r\nbelonging. Duke Student Health combines the resources of a world-class\r\nacademic institution with a deeply personal commitment to student well-being.\r\nOur providers benefit from: An integrated electronic health record system. Access to an expansive Duke specialist network for\r\n     consultation and referral. Comprehensive diagnostic and ancillary services. A robust telehealth platform. Opportunities for teaching, mentorship, scholarship,\r\n     and professional growth. A collaborative environment where every team member's\r\n     voice is valued. Duke is committed to fostering a culture where people from\r\nall backgrounds feel welcomed, respected, and empowered to contribute their\r\nunique perspectives. We believe our strongest ideas emerge when diverse\r\nexperiences, viewpoints, and talents come together. Please check out our full benefits at https://hr.duke.edu/benefits/ Physical\r\nRequirements This role is primarily office-based with occasional outdoor\r\nactivities. Duties may include standing or sitting for extended periods,\r\nwalking throughout campus facilities, using computer technology, climbing\r\nstairs, and occasionally lifting items weighing up to 50 pounds. Reasonable\r\naccommodations are available for qualified individuals. Application\r\nInformation Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the\r\nposition is filled. Anticipated Pay Range Duke University provides an annual base salary range for this position as USD $180,000 to USD $190,000. Duke University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position; candidate's work experience, education/training, and key skills; internal peer equity; as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. Ready\r\nto Make a Difference? Apply today and help foster the health, resilience, and\r\nsuccess of Duke students. Join a team committed to helping every student\r\nflourish while advancing the future of college health. Be You. Be Bold. Choose Duke. Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://students.duke.edu/wellness/studenthealth/ 114 S. Buchanan Blvd © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32664": {
      "title": "TT Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Duke University Medical Center, Biochemistry Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University Medical Center, Biochemistry Position ID: DukeUniv-Biochemistry-ASSTPROF [#32664, 51228244] Position Title: TT Assistant Professor Position Type: Tenured/Tenure-track faculty Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27710, United States of America [ map ] Subject Areas: Biochemistry / Biochemistry , Cell Biology , Cryo-electron microscopy Appl Deadline: 2026/11/01 23:59:59 * * (posted 2026/09/10 ) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Duke University Department of Biochemistry and Cell Biology invites applications for a junior tenure-track faculty position. We welcome applications from all fields of biochemistry and cell biology. Applicants whose research program studies significant biological questions at the cusp of biochemistry and cell biology by leveraging in vivo and quantitative approaches and state-of-the-art techniques such as CryoET are especially encouraged. Successful candidates will demonstrate a track record of creativity and productivity, show potential for outstanding future achievements, and have a strong desire to integrate into Duke’s collaborative and expanding research community. Responsibilities include developing a productive and innovative research program, securing external funding, and actively participating in graduate and post-graduate training and mentorship. The department has an exceptional history in biomedical research innovation that includes two Nobel Laureates, HHMI investigators, and National Academy Members. Strengths include structural biology, enzymology & biophysics, genomics, quantitative biology (Q-Bio), developmental biology, neuroscience, and AI-Bio research programs. Applicants should hold a Ph.D. in a biomedical research field relevant to this search. The application package should include a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a three-page statement of research (organized as a one-page summary of past research accomplishments and a two-page summary of your future research plans), a half-page statement of mentoring philosophy, a half-page statement of how you envision collaborating with current faculty, and 3 letters of recommendation. Please note that Duke specifically seeks information about past misconduct or policy violations (in the past ten (10) years) and/or relevant pending investigations as part of the application process. Disclosures will not be an automatic bar to hiring but, instead, will initiate further dialogue regarding past actions and steps taken to address them. Disclosures will not be shared with search committees during the application review process. Duke University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Important Dates: Applications should in their most complete form and be received by no later than November 1, 2026, for full consideration. PLEASE BE SURE TO SUBMIT 3 PAGE STATEMENT OF RESEARCH AND ALL REQUIREMENTS OF THE PACKAGE. Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Please note that Duke University specifically seeks information about past\r\nmisconduct or policy violations (in the past ten (10) years) and/or\r\nrelevant pending investigations as part of the application process.\r\nDisclosures will not be an automatic bar to hiring but, instead, will\r\ninitiate further dialogue regarding past actions and steps taken to\r\naddress them. Disclosures will not be shared with search committees\r\nduring the application review process. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Research statement Publication list mentoring philosphy (half page) statement of how you envision collaborating with current faculty (half-page) statement of future plans (half page) Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://www.biochem.duke.edu/ Biochemistry Department 307 Research Drive Box 3711, DUMC Durham, NC 27710 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33038": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Duke University Medical Center, Radiology/Center for InVivo Microscopy Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University Medical Center, Radiology/Center for InVivo Microscopy Position ID: DukeUniv-CIVM-POSTDOC [#33038, 275539] Position Title: Postdoctoral Associate Position Type: Postdoctoral Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27710, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Radiology Appl Deadline: 2026/10/23 23:59:59  (listed until 2026/10/23) Position Description: Apply Position Description School of Medicine Established in 1930, Duke University School of Medicine is the youngest of the nation's top medical schools. Ranked sixth among medical schools in the nation, the School takes pride in being an inclusive community of outstanding learners, investigators, clinicians, and staff where interdisciplinary collaboration is embraced and great ideas accelerate translation of fundamental scientific discoveries to improve human health locally and around the globe. Composed of more than 2,600 faculty physicians and researchers, nearly 2,000 students, and more than 6,200 staff, the Duke University School of Medicine along with the Duke University School of Nursing, and Duke University Health System comprise Duke Health, a world-class academic medical center. The Health System encompasses Duke University Hospital, Duke Regional Hospital, Duke Raleigh Hospital, Duke Health Integrated Practice, Duke Primary Care, Duke Home Care and Hospice, Duke Health and Wellness, and multiple affiliations.\r\nBe You. The Quantitative Imaging and Analysis Laboratory in the Department of Radiology at Duke University is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate to join our team. In this role, you will work on the development and application of advanced computed tomography methods, with a focus on photon-counting CT, quantitative image analysis, and machine learning. The position will involve work across several NIH-funded research projects in preclinical and translational imaging. Current projects include spectral photon-counting CT of cerebral vasculature and intracranial aneurysms, photon-counting CT and computational imaging of head and neck cancer, and multiorgan CT studies of aging and cardiovascular disease. The Postdoctoral Associate will have the opportunity to work on topics including: Photon-counting and spectral CT imaging\r\nCT reconstruction and image-processing methods\r\nMaterial decomposition and quantitative spectral imaging\r\nImage segmentation, registration, and quantitative morphometry\r\nMachine learning and deep learning for CT image analysis and reconstruction\r\nComputational and digital-twin models for preclinical imaging\r\nAnalysis of longitudinal and dynamic imaging data\r\nDevelopment and validation of imaging biomarkers\r\n \r\nThe work will combine method development with analysis of experimental imaging data. There will also be opportunities to participate directly in preclinical imaging studies and in the development of new imaging protocols. Minimum Requirements: Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate (e.g. Sc.D., M.D., D.V.M.) in biomedical engineering, electrical or computer engineering, medical physics, computer science, applied physics, or a closely related field. Candidates with non-US degrees may be required to provide proof of degree equivalency.\r\nNote for international candidates: Generally, immigration classifications (e.g., H-1B, J-1, etc.) require that the requisite degree be conferred before a petition can be filed or a visa document issued to sponsor the individual.\r\nPreferred Qualifications: A strong quantitative and computational background\r\nExperience in one or more of the following areas is preferred: CT or other tomographic image reconstruction, medical image analysis, machine learning or deep learning, python and/or MATLAB, scientific computing and numerical methods.\r\nExperience with computing, PyTorch, spectral CT, photon-counting detectors, or preclinical imaging would be helpful but is not required.\r\nOther Requirements: Onsite. The work is performed on-site or at a designated assignment location.\r\nBe Bold. Position Description: The conscientious discharge of research or scholarship responsibilities, which may include teaching responsibilities for Postdoctoral Associates\r\nConformance to standards of responsible conduct in research\r\nCompliance with good scholarly and research practice\r\nMaintenance of a laboratory notebook and/or other comparable records of research activity, which remains the property of Duke University upon termination\r\nAdherence to University standards regarding use of isotopes, chemicals, infectious agents, animals, human subjects, and the like\r\nOpen and timely discussion with the mentor regarding all facets of the Postdoctoral Appointee's research activities. Postdoctoral Appointees are encouraged to consult the AAMC Compact Between Postdoctoral Appointees and Their Mentors for suggested guidelines for the Postdoctoral Appointee-mentor relationship\r\nPrompt disclosure to the mentor regarding the possession and desire to distribute materials, reagents, software, copyrightable and potentially patentable discoveries derived from the Postdoctoral Appointee's research.\r\nCollegial conduct towards members of the research group and others as described in the Duke University School of Medicine Honor Code of Professional Conduct and other relevant conduct policies pertaining to other schools at Duke University.\r\nCompliance with all applicable University and departmental policies and procedures.\r\nChoose Duke. Join our award-winning team and be part of an inclusive culture that values excellence, innovation, and discovery. Duke University is consistently ranked among the top universities worldwide and is renowned for its cutting-edge research across disciplines. Beyond the engaging work, you'll also benefit from Duke's competitive benefits package, including health insurance plans, generous paid time off, retirement programs with employer contributions, tuition assistance for employees and their children, and more. Screening of Applications: Screening continues until position is filled. Job Code: 00003820 POSTDOCTORAL ASSOCIATE\r\nJob Level: 00 Duke is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment opportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy related conditions), sexual orientation or military status. Duke aspires to create a community built on collaboration, innovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich diversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. To achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the community feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all individuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Essential Physical Job Functions:\r\nCertain jobs at Duke University and Duke University Health System may include essential job functions that require specific physical and/or mental abilities. Additional information and provision for requests for reasonable accommodation will be provided by each hiring department. Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Research statement Publication list Reference letter (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site. Letters should be submitted by 2026/10/24 11:59PM ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://careers.duke.edu/job-invite/275539/ 919-684-7755 Duke University Medical Center Bryan Research Building 311 Research Dr., Room 141 Durham, NC 27710 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33216": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Duke University, Biology Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Biology Position ID: Duke-Biology-PD_SL [#33216] Position Title: Postdoctoral Associate Position Type: Postdoctoral Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Biology Appl Deadline: (posted 2026/10/23 , updated 2026/10/26 , listed until 2027/04/23) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Lipshutz Lab in the Department of Biology at Duke University is seeking a full-time Postdoctoral Associate to join a research program focused on understanding the impact of sensory pollutants on songbird behavior, physiology and fitness. The Lipshutz Lab conducts research on sexual selection, speciation, and sensory ecology in songbirds and shorebirds. Major areas of research include identifying the genomic basis of reproductive isolation, hormonal and neuro-transcriptomic mechanisms of aggression and parental care, and behavioral and physiological responses to anthropogenic sensory pollution. To support these efforts, the postdoctoral associate will perform a variety of molecular laboratory procedures including nucleotide and hormone isolation, PCR, and enzyme immunoassay, as well as field ornithology procedures including mist-netting, banding, and blood sampling. The researcher will work closely with the PI and other lab members to support ongoing projects and develop independent research skills. Applicants should be motivated, dependable, highly organized, and able to work effectively within a collaborative research environment. Strong communication skills and careful attention to detail are essential. Minimum requirements: PhD in biology or a related field. Prior research experience in molecular labwork as well as fieldwork is highly desirable. The position is available beginning April 1, 2026, with flexible start dates based on candidate availability. For more information, visit the Lipshutz Lab website: https://saralipshutz.wordpress.com/ Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: www.biology.duke.edu 137 Biological Sciences Bldg. Box 90338 Durham NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33217": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Duke University, Biology Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Biology Position ID: Duke-Biology-RA_AMV [#33217] Position Title: Research Associate Position Type: Other Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Biology Appl Deadline: (posted 2026/10/23 , listed until 2027/04/23) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Mazo-Vargas laboratory in Duke University’s Department of Biology seeks a part-time Research Associate to support next-generation sequencing projects in Lepidoptera developmental genetics and evolution. The successful candidate will prepare and evaluate RNA-seq, ATAC-seq, and ChIP-seq libraries; perform quality control and genomic data analysis; maintain clear experimental and computational records; and contribute to data interpretation. The candidate may also help optimize genomic workflows and support undergraduate and graduate researchers. A PhD in molecular biology, genetics, genomics, developmental biology, bioinformatics, or a related field is required. Experience with next-generation sequencing and genomic data analysis is expected. Familiarity with R, Python, command-line tools, high-performance computing, and reproducible workflows is preferred. This is a part-time position of approximately 20–30 hours per week for at least six months. The position is based at Duke University in Durham, North Carolina, and will begin as soon as possible. Questions may be directed to Dr. Anyi Mazo-Vargas at anyi.mv@duke.edu Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: www.biology.duke.edu 137 Biological Sciences Bldg. Box 90338 Durham NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33215": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Duke University, Biology Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Biology Position ID: Duke-Biology-RA_RB [#33215] Position Title: Research Associate Position Type: Other Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Biology Appl Deadline: (posted 2026/10/23 , listed until 2027/04/23) Position Description: Apply Position Description A full-time research position is available in the Baugh lab in the Department of Biology at Duke University. The Baugh lab uses the roundworm C. elegans to study nutritional control of development and organismal physiology. The Research Associate will contribute to projects investigating adult consequences of early life starvation and nutritional control of gene expression. Substantial research experience is necessary. Skills related to genetic analysis, molecular biology, imaging, and computational analysis are critical, and experience with nematodes is ideal. This position is part of a research team, and training and mentoring will be provided. Please start the filename for your cover letter and CV with your last name. This position requires a PhD. Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: www.biology.duke.edu 137 Biological Sciences Bldg. Box 90338 Durham NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33218": {
      "title": "Research Associate/Director of Research & Outreach",
      "description": "Duke University, Fuqua School of Business (Faculty) Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Fuqua School of Business (Faculty) Position ID: Duke-Fuqua School of Business (Faculty)-RAVTRL [#33218] Position Title: Research Associate/Director of Research & Outreach Position Type: Other Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Management and Organizations Appl Deadline: 2026/10/30 23:59:59  (posted 2026/10/23 ) Position Description: Apply Position Description Duke University's Fuqua School of Business invites applications for the position of Research Associate and Director of Research & Outreach, expected to begin December 1, 2026. This is initially a 12-month position with the possibility of renewal or extension contingent on satisfactory performance, continued programmatic need, and availability of funding. The Director of Research & Outreach will lead the day-to-day implementation of the Veteran Transitions Research Lab (VTRL) at Duke University’s Fuqua School of Business. Working closely with VTRL’s faculty leadership, the Director will manage and contribute to VTRL’s research portfolio, coordinate external partnerships and programs, lead research-to-practice and convening activities, and support the Lab’s long-term growth and sustainability. Primary responsibilities: \r\n• Manage and contribute to VTRL’s portfolio of original research, including study planning, participant recruitment, data collection, project timelines, and deliverables.\r\n• Develop and coordinate scholarly and applied research products, including reports, evidence syntheses, and research summaries.\r\n• Manage VTRL’s affiliated researcher network, scholar-support initiatives, and related research programs.\r\n• Lead the planning and execution of the VTRL Annual Summit and other convenings.\r\n• Coordinate relationships and activities with affiliated researchers, employers, veteran-serving organizations, funders, policymakers, and other external partners.\r\n• Support the dissemination and translation of research findings for academic, practitioner, and partner audiences.\r\n• Coordinate research compliance, partnership agreements, and related administrative processes with appropriate Duke offices and external partners.\r\n• Support external funding, proposal development, sponsor and donor engagement, and long-term sustainability planning.\r\n• Supervise assigned personnel and coordinate the work of affiliated researchers, consultants, collaborators, and project-supported scholars as appropriate. Required qualifications: \r\n• PhD in social psychology, organizational behavior, management, or a closely related behavioral or social science field by the position start date.\r\n• Demonstrated experience designing, conducting, and interpreting behavioral, organizational, management, or related social science research.\r\n• Demonstrated ability to manage complex research projects and coordinate work across multiple collaborators or stakeholder groups.\r\n• Knowledge of human-subjects research and experience working with research compliance processes.\r\n• Excellent written and oral communication skills, including the ability to communicate scientific findings to academic and practitioner audiences.\r\n• Strong organizational skills, judgment, initiative, and ability to work effectively with a high degree of independence.\r\n• Experience supervising, mentoring, or coordinating the work of staff, students, researchers, or collaborators. For full consideration, applications should be submitted by October 30, 2026. Applicants should submit their materials electronically at: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33218 Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Transcript or diploma of highest degree Two reference letters (to be submitted online by the reference writers on this site ) Further Info: Fuqua School of Business 100 Fuqua Drive Duke University, Box 90120 Durham NC  27708-0120 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33131": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of the Practice",
      "description": "Duke University, International Comparative Studies Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, International Comparative Studies Position ID: Duke-International Comparative Studies-APOP [#33131, 51085075] Position Title: Assistant Professor of the Practice Position Type: Non tenure-track faculty Position Location: durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: International Comparative Studies Appl Deadline: 2026/12/14 23:59:59 * (posted 2026/10/19 , listed until 2026/12/14) Position Description: Apply Position Description The International Comparative Studies Program at Duke University in Durham, North Carolina invites applications for an Assistant Professor of the Practice that begins July 1, 2027, and ends June 1, 2031. This is a regular-rank renewable faculty position with an initial four-year term. We seek a candidate whose research is at the intersection of Global Studies and Science and Technology Studies. The successful candidate will bring interdisciplinary and critical approaches to understanding how technologies fuel and are shaped by global circulations of capital and labor, empire, surveillance, migration, supply chains, humanitarian projects, activism and resistance, embodiment, or other themes consistent with the mission, learning outcomes, and curriculum of International Comparative Studies, as described below. International Comparative Studies ( https://internationalcomparative.duke.edu ) is an undergraduate interdisciplinary program that bridges the humanities and social sciences. Students pursue a Global Studies major that focuses on one of seven world regions (Africa, China and East Asia, Russia and Central Asia, South Asia, Latin America and the Caribbean, Middle East, and Europe) through language acquisition, area studies course work, and interdisciplinary courses. The successful candidate will have completed a Ph.D. in the humanities and/or social sciences prior to appointment, be engaged in research and teaching that explores transregional institutions, discourses, and relationships, and be interested in pursuing interdisciplinary and cross-regional collaborations. The selected candidate will demonstrate interest in teaching core ICS courses as well as courses that incorporate digital research methods, and will supervise senior theses, work effectively with students and colleagues, and contribute appropriate service in the program, including undergraduate advising and mentoring and active participation in curriculum-building. Possible disciplines include human geography, socio-cultural anthropology, transnational or global history, environmental studies, women and gender studies, cultural studies, and global media studies. Candidates who conduct research in one or more of the seven regions in which ICS students concentrate will be given priority. The position carries a 2/2 teaching load with expectation that one course will be in the candidate’s area of specialization. To apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, a writing sample or publication of no more than 28 pages, a one-page teaching statement, and one syllabus for a class you have taught (courses with an interdisciplinary and/or global scope will be especially relevant). In addition, the names and contact information of three recommenders must be submitted with the application. We will only request letters if you are shortlisted. All material should be submitted electronically through the following link: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33131 . Applications received by December 14, 2026 are guaranteed consideration. If you have questions please contact the Chair of the committee, Professor Jessica Namakkal or ICS Business Manager, Briani Meyers. Duke is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment opportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy-related conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke aspires to create a community built on collaboration, innovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich diversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. To achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the community feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all individuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Please note that Duke specifically seeks information about past misconduct or policy violations (in the past ten (10) years) and/or relevant pending investigations as part of the application process. Disclosures will not be an automatic bar to hiring but, instead, will initiate further dialogue regarding past actions and steps taken to address them. Disclosures will not be shared with search committees during the application review process. Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Please note that Duke University specifically seeks information about past\r\nmisconduct or policy violations (in the past ten (10) years) and/or\r\nrelevant pending investigations as part of the application process.\r\nDisclosures will not be an automatic bar to hiring but, instead, will\r\ninitiate further dialogue regarding past actions and steps taken to\r\naddress them. Disclosures will not be shared with search committees\r\nduring the application review process. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: https://internationalcomparative.duke.edu/ 1304 campus dr box 90405 durham nc 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33236": {
      "title": "Associate in Research",
      "description": "Duke University, Mechanical Engineering and Materials Science Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Mechanical Engineering and Materials Science Position ID: Duke-MEMS-AIRARYA [#33236] Position Title: Associate in Research Position Type: Other Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27701, United States of America [ map ] Subject Areas: Engineering / Materials Science and Engineering , Mechanical Engineering Appl Deadline: 2026/11/03 23:59:59  (posted 2026/10/26 , listed until 2026/11/03) Position Description: Apply Position Description Duke University was created in\r\n1924 through an indenture of trust by James Buchanan Duke. Today, Duke is regarded as one of America’s leading research universities. Located in Durham, North Carolina,\r\nDuke is positioned in the heart of the Research Triangle, which is ranked\r\nannually as one of the best places in the country to work and live. Duke has more than 15,000\r\nstudents who study and conduct research in its 10 undergraduate, graduate and\r\nprofessional schools. With about 40,000 employees, Duke is the third largest\r\nprivate employer in North Carolina, and it now has international programs in\r\nmore than 150 countries. The Pratt School of\r\nEngineering at Duke University is one of the fastest rising, highly ranked\r\nengineering schools in the nation. The school consists of four departments with\r\n130 tenure-track faculty members, 1250 undergraduate students, 1400 master’s students,\r\nand 600 PhD students. Housed within a university renowned for its programs in\r\nthe liberal arts, medicine, business and law, Pratt prepares future engineering leaders to address complex challenges with solutions\r\nthat take into account the complexities and nuances of implementing them. Pratt\r\ntakes a whole-student approach to\r\neducation, ensuring students are\r\nwell supported throughout their journeys and graduate with the grit and\r\ndetermination required to persevere in their careers and their lives. Pratt is\r\ndedicated to the values of diversity, equitability, inclusivity and community\r\nin its pursuit of knowledge and service to society. Occupational Summary An individual with academic\r\ncredentials but without a doctorate and not a degree candidate. Assists faculty\r\nmembers in research programs by participating in the research directly or in\r\norganizing a program under which the research is carried out. This classification is administered on Campus through the Office of the Provost and in the Medical Center throughout the office of the Chancellor for Health Affairs. Is it not subject to the Wage and\r\nSalary system. Work Performed Shock wave lithotripsy (SWL) is\r\na non-invasive technique for fragmenting kidney stones. Our previous research\r\nhas demonstrated the critical role of stress waves and cavitation in stone\r\nfragmentation. Yet, the synergistic interaction between these two contributing mechanisms have not been explored, which can further improve the treatment\r\nefficiency of SWL. This project will explore the\r\ninterplay between surface acoustic waves, triggered by the incident shock waves, and cavitation erosion produced by the collapse of cavitation bubbles near the stone surface. The primary responsibilities for this position will be to work on mechanical design using CAD software, 3D printing and/or CNC machining, acoustic pressure measurements, shock wave lithotripsy on stone phantoms, image\r\nacquisition and analysis. This\r\nposition offers flexibility in schedule, with an anticipated commitment of 20\r\nhours per week. Minimum Qualifications Education The applicant should have a MS degree in ME or\r\nBME. Experience The applicant should have experience using CAD software, 3D printing and/or CNC\r\nmachining, acoustic pressure measurements, and image acquisition and analysis Skills The applicant should have\r\nthe skills required for using CAD software, 3D printing and/or\r\nCNC machining, acoustic pressure measurements, and image acquisition and\r\nanalysis. The intent of this job description is to provide a representative and level of the types of\r\nduties and responsibilities that will be required of the positions given this title and shall not be construed as\r\na declaration of the total of the specific duties and responsibilities of any\r\nparticular position. Employees may be directed to perform job-related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description. Duke is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity\r\nEmployer committed to providing employment opportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic\r\ninformation, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or\r\nveteran status. Duke aspires to create a community built on\r\ncollaboration, innovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success\r\ndepends on the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich\r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. To achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the community feel secure\r\nand welcome, that the contributions of all individuals are respected, and that\r\nall voices are heard. All members of our community have a responsibility to\r\nuphold these values. Essential Physical Job Functions Certain\r\njobs at Duke University and Duke University Health System may include essential\r\njob functions that require specific\r\nphysical and/or mental abilities. Additional\r\ninformation and provision for requests for reasonable accommodation will be provided by each hiring department. Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: www.mems.duke.edu 919-660-5310 Duke University Thomas Lord Department of Mechanical Engineering & Materials Science Box 90300 Durham, NC  27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/33163": {
      "title": "Part-time Instructor",
      "description": "Duke University, Music Department Skip to main content AcademicJobsOnline .org ‌ View Jobs Events Registered Employers Contact Us Login Duke University, Music Department Position ID: Duke-Music Department-NRRDJEMBE [#33163] Position Title: Part-time Instructor Position Type: Non-regular rank faculty Position Location: Durham, North Carolina 27708, United States of America [ map ] Subject Area: Music / percussion Appl Deadline: 2026/11/20 23:59:59 * * (posted 2026/10/20 ) Position Description: Apply Position Description The Department of Music at Duke University seeks to hire a part-time instructor to teach djembe drumming to music majors, minors, and non-majors. Two hours per week of instruction will be offered in a small class setting. Candidates should have an established career as a teacher and performer. A master's degree or higher, or equivalent professional experience, is required. This is a one-semester non-regular rank position, with the possibility of renewal. Please submit a CV and cover letter by November 20, 2026. Duke University\r\n is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to providing employment \r\nopportunity without regard to an individual's age, color, disability, \r\ngender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, \r\nnational origin, ethnicity, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy and pregnancy \r\nrelated conditions), sexual orientation, or military status. Duke University aspires to create a community built on collaboration, \r\ninnovation, creativity, and belonging. Our collective success depends on\r\n the robust exchange of ideas—an exchange that is best when the rich \r\ndiversity of our perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences flourishes. \r\nTo achieve this exchange, it is essential that all members of the \r\ncommunity feel secure and welcome, that the contributions of all \r\nindividuals are respected, and that all voices are heard. All members of\r\n our community have a responsibility to uphold these values. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae And anything else requested in the position description. Further Info: music.duke.edu 919-660-3310 Duke University Department of Music PO Box 90665 Durham, NC 27708 © 2026 AcademicJobsOnline.Org. All Rights Reserved."
